meta {
  name: List catalogue page
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/catalog?category=clothes&offset=0&limit=6
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  category: clothes
  offset: 0
  limit: 6
}

docs {
  # List catalogue page

  Returns one page of the product catalogue, optionally filtered to one
  category. Backs the mobile Catalog view (category chips, product grid and
  "Show more products"). Unlike `GET /api/v1/products`, it carries each
  product's category and no store location.

  Products come from the external demo feed
  (`https://api.escuelajs.co/api/v1/products`). The feed does not report a
  total, so the server asks it for `limit + 1` products and reports whether
  the extra one exists as `hasMore`. Clients page by adding the number of
  products received to `offset`; the feed can change between two requests,
  so a client should drop any product whose `id` it already shows.

  ## Caching

  Each distinct feed URL (category, offset and size) is cached in process for
  **5 minutes**. The category list used to resolve `category` has its own
  5-minute cache. Failures are never cached.

  ## Auth

  None. This endpoint is public.

  ## Parameters

  - `category` (query, string, optional) — a `slug` from
    `GET /api/v1/categories`. Omit it for every category. Must appear at most
    once and must not be empty.
  - `offset` (query, integer, optional, default `0`) — products to skip.
    Plain digits only, `0`–`10000`.
  - `limit` (query, integer, optional, default `12`) — page size. Plain digits
    only, `1`–`24`.

  ## Responses

  ### 200 OK

  {
    "products": [
      {
        "id": 4,
        "name": "Classic Grey Hooded Sweatshirt",
        "category": "Clothes",
        "priceAud": 90,
        "imageUrl": "https://i.imgur.com/R2PN9Wq.jpeg"
      }
    ],
    "offset": 0,
    "limit": 6,
    "hasMore": true
  }

  - `products` (array) — at most `limit` products, feed order.
  - `products[].id` (number) — feed identifier.
  - `products[].name` (string) — product name.
  - `products[].category` (string) — category name; empty when the feed has none.
  - `products[].priceAud` (number) — price, assumed AUD (see `GET /api/v1/products`).
  - `products[].imageUrl` (string) — first image; empty when the feed has none.
  - `offset`, `limit` (number) — the values applied.
  - `hasMore` (boolean) — whether another page exists after this one.

  ### 400 Bad Request — invalid parameter

  `offset` or `limit` is not plain digits or is out of range, or `category`
  is empty or repeated. The feed is not contacted.

  {
    "statusCode": 400,
    "error": "Bad Request",
    "message": "Parameter \"limit\" must be between 1 and 24.",
    "validation": [],
    "url": "/api/v1/catalog?limit=25",
    "method": "GET"
  }

  ### 404 Not Found — unknown category

  {
    "statusCode": 404,
    "error": "Not Found",
    "message": "Category \"nope\" does not exist.",
    "validation": [],
    "url": "/api/v1/catalog?category=nope",
    "method": "GET"
  }

  ### 502 Bad Gateway — catalogue source unavailable

  The product feed failed, or a `category` was given and the category list
  could not be read (the filter cannot be resolved).

  {
    "statusCode": 502,
    "error": "Bad Gateway",
    "message": "The product catalogue source is unavailable.",
    "validation": [],
    "url": "/api/v1/catalog",
    "method": "GET"
  }
}
